course: dictionary
lesson: 15870
title: Word parts: un- means not
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word unheated has two parts: un- and heated. The part un- at the start of a word often means not or without. Heated means warmed by a heater, a fire or the sun. So unheated means not heated, or without any heating.
explain: «The garage is unheated, so it is freezing in winter.» The clue is freezing: a place with no heating stays cold. Try the swap check: «The garage is not heated, so it is freezing in winter» still makes sense, so unheated must mean not heated.
explain: Other words with un- work the same way: unlocked, unkind and unopened. Once you know that un- often means not, you can work out many new words quickly. Always check your meaning in the sentence to be sure it fits.
fact: The prefix un- at the start of a word often means not or without.
fact: «Unheated» means without any heating, so it stays cold.
fact: «An unheated pool» is an outdoor pool with no heater, so the water can be chilly.
fact: In science, unheated water stays at room temperature.
fact: Experiments often compare heated and unheated samples to see what the heat changes.
exercise: «The conservatory was unheated all winter.» What does unheated mean? | Very noisy | Full of plants and bright sunshine | Heated by a big fire | *Without any heating, so it stayed cold
exercise: «We swam in the unheated outdoor pool in June.» What does unheated tell you about the pool? | *It had no heating, so the water was not warmed | It had a glass roof over it | It had no heater, so the water stayed cool | It was as hot as a bath
exercise: Find and copy the word that means not heated: «The unheated garage was full of old bikes.» | *unheated | full | bikes | garage
test: In «Poor families lived in unheated homes in winter», what does unheated mean? | Painted bright blue | Very large | *Without any heating | Warm and cosy
test: In the word unheated, what does the prefix un- mean? | Under | *Not or without | Again | Very or extremely
exam: An experiment compares a heated sample and an unheated sample of water. What is the unheated sample like? | It turns to ice straight away | It boils at once | *It stays at room temperature | It becomes sweet
